            "target_entity_instance": "Yasso07 model",
            "target_entity_type": "SourceComponent",
            "paragraph": "Soil C dynamics are simulated using Yasso07 model (Tuomi et al. 2011). Soil C pools are fed from C loss from the vegetation pools in JSBACH and divided to four factions: water solubles, ethanol solubles, acid hydrolysables, and compounds neither soluble nor hydrolysable. C is further divided to woody and non-woody litter and above and belowground partitions. The Yasso model is then used to simulate organic matter decomposition in soil based on the litter chemical properties, weather conditions and physical size of the litter.",
