        {
            "source_entity_instance": "heatwave",
            "source_entity_type": "Weather_Event",
            "relation": "IMPACTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Finland",
            "target_entity_type": "Country",
            "paragraph": "Finnish urban ecosystems are affected by both the rapid warming of northern regions (Rantanen et al. 2022) and the urban climate properties \u2013 a combination which exacerbates the changes in the future meteorological conditions and makes urban ecosystems susceptible to extreme weather, like drought. Previous studies have shown that, for example, drought stress can be especially significant in the urban context due to elevated temperatures resulting from the UHI effect (Warner et al. 2024). Even in the current climate, many urban green spaces are irrigated to alleviate the effects of drought. In previous research, irrigation is found to increase photosynthetic uptake during dry periods and enhance the cooling potential of vegetation (Th\u00f6lix et al. 2025; Ignatieva et al. 2020).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
